# Renovate's settings for scripts/renovate.sh, run by the `renovate` user on the dev machine. Copy to
# $YGG_SECRETS_DIR/renovate.env (default /etc/yggdrasil-renovate/renovate.env; `ygg install` does it),
# chmod 600, owned by renovate, and fill in. Never commit the copy.
#
# The file goes to Docker as an --env-file, which reads each line literally: NAME=value, no quotes, no
# `export`, no comments after a value (put them on lines of their own, as here). It is not shell.

# The Forgejo token of the `renovate` user: write:repository (it pushes renovate/* branches), write:issue
# (pull requests, the dependency dashboard), read:user (Renovate asks Forgejo who it is when it starts; without
# it the run fails with "Authentication failure") and read:organization. Required. The token is only ever in
# this file and in the run-scoped copy scripts/renovate.sh makes for the container (mode 600, removed after
# the run).
RENOVATE_TOKEN=

# Forgejo's REST API: https://git.<DOMAIN>/api/v1 (the forge url of catalog.yaml plus /api/v1). Left empty,
# renovate.sh asks the catalog.
RENOVATE_ENDPOINT=

# Forgejo is Renovate's `gitea` platform. renovate.sh refuses anything else here.
RENOVATE_PLATFORM=gitea

# Renovate visits only the repositories renovate.sh lists (the catalog's applications and repositories,
# under the catalog's owner), never everything the token can see. renovate.sh refuses anything but false.
RENOVATE_AUTODISCOVER=false

# Not here: RENOVATE_REPOSITORIES and RENOVATE_CONFIG. renovate.sh computes them on every run, and refuses a
# file that has them (a stale list would visit repositories the catalog no longer has).

# Optional: a GitHub token, for the release notes and changelogs Renovate puts in its pull requests. Without
# one it asks GitHub anonymously, from this one address, and runs into the rate limit (machine check warns).
# A fine-grained personal access token with no permissions at all, read-only access to public repositories
# only, is enough. renovate.sh gives it to Renovate as GITHUB_COM_TOKEN, through the run-scoped env file like
# RENOVATE_TOKEN (never as an argument), and never prints it. Leave it empty to run without.
RENOVATE_GITHUB_COM_TOKEN=
